# CLAUDE.md Template

> 한국어 버전: [templates/CLAUDE.md.example](../CLAUDE.md.example)

Copy this file to your project root as `CLAUDE.md` and fill it in for your project.
Claude Code reads this file automatically at the start of each session.

---

# Project Name

Explain in one or two paragraphs what the project does.
Say who uses it and what its core features are.

## Common Commands

```bash
npm install        # Install dependencies
npm test           # Run the full test suite
npm run test:unit  # Unit tests only
npm run lint       # Lint check
npm run dev        # Run the local dev server
```

## Directory Structure

```
src/
  api/        # HTTP handlers — no business logic, only service calls
  services/   # Business logic
  models/     # DB models and migrations
  utils/      # Shared utilities
tests/        # Mirrors the src/ structure
```

## Environment Setup

```bash
./scripts/setup.sh   # Installs dependencies + creates .env + runs a health check, all in one
```

- See `.env.example` for the required environment variables. Tests run without real secret values.
- If setup fails, check your Node version (against `.nvmrc`).

## Coding Conventions

- camelCase for functions/variables, PascalCase for types/classes
- Throw errors as `AppError` subclasses; catch only in the handler layer
- Every new feature must ship with tests
- Write comments only to explain the "why"

## Caveats

- `src/legacy/` is mid-migration — do not add new code there
- DB migrations must always go in a separate PR
- Do not edit `config/production.ts`; it is managed by the deploy pipeline
